        ":question/id": "8d476a50-5742-5b02-8acf-300d458d3177",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int {x}^{8}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the power rule with $n=8$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{8}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{8+1}}{8+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{9}}{9}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{9}}{9}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{9}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{9})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 9{x}^{8} & = \\\\ {x}^{8}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$"
